WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.940
- Thanks to ExpressVPN for keeping

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:04.100
Legal Eagle safe and in the air.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.770
Despite the dire situation
that the world is experiencing

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.530
because of the COVID-19 pandemic,

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.130
some people just have to be jerks,

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.780
like this guy, Larz, a
California, quote, "influencer"

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.780
who thought it would be
cute to lick a toilet

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.882
and dub it the coronavirus challenge.

00:00:19.882 --> 00:00:21.882
- Coronavirus challenge!

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:26.490
- He later ended up in the
hospital with coronavirus.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.600
Larz inspired people like Ava Louise

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.520
to lick a toilet seat herself,

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.730
and this other guy, Cody Lee Pfister,

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.160
filmed himself licking a
row of deodorant at Walmart.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.270
- Who's scared of coronavirus?

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.420
Don't touch your mouth.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:41.950
- Pfister was arrested,

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.160
or this group of Cincinnati
residents who flouted

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.650
the governor's social distancing orders

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.860
by throwing a coronavirus party.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.530
The legal term for these people is idiots,

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.630
and what do all of these
idiots have in common,

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:55.380
besides being nominees for
the 2020 Darwin Awards?

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.950
They may have done
things that could result

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.655
in lawsuits or even jail time.

00:00:59.655 --> 00:01:02.488
(dramatic music)

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.040
Hey legal eagles, it's
time to think like a lawyer

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.350
because today we're gonna talk about

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.360
a bunch of different cases where people

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.900
intentionally or knowingly expose others

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.630
to the novel coronavirus.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.370
What happens when someone pulls a prank

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.000
and coughs on the salad bar?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.150
Is it a criminal offense
to give someone COVID-19?

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.460
And what happens if you
intentionally try to infect others?

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:25.960
I'm here to answer all of these questions

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.260
and scare you away from ever
eating at a restaurant again.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.760
Now, let's start with the
basics of assault and battery.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.810
Most causes of action
for spreading COVID-19

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.370
would probably be on the state level

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:36.650
starting with assault and battery,

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.550
which are both tort claims
and criminal offenses.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:42.100
The same conduct can lead
to a personal injury lawsuit

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.130
and a criminal prosecution,
depending on who initiates

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.950
the case and the severity of the actions

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.210
that we're talking about here.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:51.300
Battery is generally defined
as a harmful or offensive

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.530
contact with another person's body.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.630
Now, the victim's body
under this definition

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:57.380
is usually extended to include things

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.920
that the victim is attached to.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.840
This is called the
extended personality rule.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.890
This means grabbing someone's shirt

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.360
or yanking their necklace
or spitting in their cup

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.320
can also be battery,
even if the perpetrator

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.770
never actually touches the victim's body.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:12.550
Now, purposefully spreading
a disease to another person

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:14.090
generally fits within the definition

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:16.230
of a harmful or offensive touching.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.410
It's certainly not
something that people want

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:19.590
in their everyday lives.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.210
For example, in
Pennsylvania a malicious man

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:25.110
in a grocery store was arrested
after deliberately coughing

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.900
in the face of an older
gentleman wearing a face mask

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.610
and gloves because of the
potential fatal risk of COVID-19.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.780
This jerk, or idiot, as we
say in the legal profession,

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.320
allegedly coughed and mocked the man

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.300
and told him that he was
now infected with the virus.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.830
This guy was also charged with
making terroristic threats

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.390
as well as battery, and we'll talk about

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.490
the terrorism charges in just a second.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:47.370
Now, similarly, assault is
usually lumped in with battery,

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.120
but it's technically a separate offense.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.690
It's usually the intentional
act that causes another person

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.440
to fear that they're about
to suffer physical harm.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.760
If a person is placed in
imminent fear of bodily harm,

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.120
this is punishable as a crime
or again as a tort as well.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.010
Imagine you're playing
pool with someone in a bar

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.945
and that person gets angry and
swings their pool cue at you.

00:03:04.945 --> 00:03:08.310
In most places in America,
if they make contact,

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:11.820
it's battery, but if they swing
and miss, that is assault,

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.340
and you guessed it, this can apply

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.190
to spreading COVID-19 as well.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.540
For example, in Maryland a
man named William Eddings

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.040
was charged with second degree assault

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.390
and four counts of
exposure by an individual

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.800
who has an infectious disease
in violation of state law

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.610
after he got in an altercation

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.220
with one of his father's tenants,

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.690
screaming and chasing
the man into his vehicle,

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:33.700
where Eddings spit on his arm twice.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.620
When police arrived, Eddings
said he had tested positive

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.980
for COVID-19 and then
spat at the officers.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.810
Again, not a smart guy here.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:43.410
Now, under Maryland law,
assault is defined as an attempt

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.020
to make an offensive contact with another

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.990
or intentionally
frightening another person.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.750
Eddings' saliva actually
hit the victim's arm,

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.380
which is definitely a battery,

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.830
and although his spit didn't
make contact with the officers,

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.110
spitting in their direction
is a clear attempt

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:59.010
to scare them and that was
enough for the assault charge.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:02.420
And in this generation
where we're worried about

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.840
droplets of water in the air,

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.740
it could be argued that
even if the main spit,

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.410
and it's ridiculous that I have to go down

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.960
to this fact situation,
but even if the main wad

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.490
didn't make contact, even
the droplets in the air

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:18.320
might qualify as a battery itself.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.610
And since assault and
battery are also torts,

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.630
it's conceivable that someone
like Eddings could be sued

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.220
for assault and battery in state court

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.810
and pay civil damages to the victims here.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.740
And Maryland, like many other states,

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.050
have specific statutes that actually deal

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.830
with the intentional spreading
of infectious diseases,

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.670
and that's one of the things
that this guy was charged with.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.270
But I mentioned terroristic threats,

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:40.720
and these days most states
have a criminal offense

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.170
called terroristic threats,

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.080
and this offense is probably not the thing

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.150
you're thinking of when you
hear the word terrorist.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.380
It has nothing to do
with foreign governments

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.430
or international elements.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.550
This is generally a
verbal or written threat

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:55.600
to commit an act meant to
terrorize another party.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.250
When you do that, you can get
arrested, not surprisingly.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.250
The threat can be paired
with an actual crime,

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.010
like battery or murder, but it
can also be a general threat

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.130
meant to terrorize.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.560
So for example, if you
called up your high school

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.170
and made a bomb threat, for instance,

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:10.740
if there was no specific statute
dealing with bomb threats,

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.210
you'd probably be charged with
making terroristic threats,

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:16.310
even if no one was in
actual physical apprehension

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:19.040
of physical contact, which
would be required for assault.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.260
Unfortunately, there are
many examples of people

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.590
doing really stupid and dangerous things

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.940
during this pandemic
that probably give rise

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:28.110
to a crime of terroristic threats.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:31.500
For example, a New Jersey
man was arrested for coughing

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.070
on a Wegmans employee,
and telling the woman that

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.810
he had the coronavirus.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.700
The employee said that
she was concerned that

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:39.510
he was standing too
close to the salad bar,

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.450
and she asked him to move.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.450
He then coughed on her and laughed,

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.120
and claimed that he had the virus.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.110
He was charged with making
a terroristic threat.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:50.600
He was also charged with
obstruction and harassment.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.160
A Texas teenager posted
several videos claiming that

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.960
she had the COVID-19 infection,

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:58.230
and wanted to kill people with it.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:00.843
- If you wanna get the coronavirus,

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:05.463
woo that, call me.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:10.540
And I will meet you up, and
(coughs) all up (coughs)

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:11.373
all over you.

00:06:11.373 --> 00:06:13.150
- Obviously, the police were concerned,

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:14.550
and they tracked her down.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:16.680
Now, this is not without controversy.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.530
The terrorism laws were intended to apply

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:23.080
to terroristic acts to a group of people,

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:25.090
and generally were not meant to apply

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:30.090
to a single individual person
talking to another person.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:33.780
But generally, true threats
are not considered free speech

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.920
and not protected by the First Amendment,

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.640
though it's still
controversial as to whether

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.570
these statements constitute
a true threat or not,

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.550
so it sort of begs the question,

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:45.420
which I'm actually using
the correct way this time.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.300
But there is precedent for
using state terroristic threats

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.100
to prosecute people for exposing others

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.290
to infectious diseases.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:53.110
Prosecutors charged
individuals with making

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:55.090
terroristic threats for
exposing their sexual partners

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:59.590
to HIV in the 1990s
which led to new statutes

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:02.640
specifically directed
towards infectious diseases.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:05.030
According to the Center
for HIV Law and Policy,

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:07.610
roughly 2/3 of states have
laws that make it a crime

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:09.890
to knowingly expose others to HIV,

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:11.920
among other infectious diseases.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:14.580
For example, in April
2012, a 19-year-old man

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.390
who had HIV was charged with assault

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:18.710
and battery with a deadly
weapon, among other things,

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:20.720
for failing to disclose his HIV status

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.430
to multiple sexual partners.

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:25.560
At least one of his partners
later tested positive for HIV.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.090
At least 12 states have
added hepatitis C to the list

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.510
of diseases that could
cause criminal prosecution

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:33.610
if the infected person
knowingly exposes other people,

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:35.510
though public health
advocates believe legislators

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.430
should be cautious about passing more laws

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:38.630
criminalizing the spread of disease,

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:42.010
because it can also stigmatize
testing and treatment.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:44.390
There are probably fewer
issues with adding COVID-19

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:45.910
to the list of diseases that are covered

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:49.100
by these disclosure laws,
since COVID-19 is easier

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.330
to transmit than hepatitis C or HIV,

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.380
and COVID-19 arguably gives
prosecutors a better argument

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.690
for aggressively charging
people who threaten to expose

00:07:56.690 --> 00:08:00.010
others to the virus because
of its ease of communication.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:02.770
Now, the state of mind
here is always important.

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:05.190
Almost all criminal laws have
a mental state requirement

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:08.030
or mens rea, or guilty mind, component.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:09.660
You can't be criminally prosecuted

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.720
just because you accidentally
infected someone.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.830
You have to intentionally
or knowingly infect them

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:17.530
in situations that give rise to liability.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.030
So don't think that anyone who happens

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:22.020
to communicate the disease is going

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.860
to be prosecuted under these laws.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:26.920
But where there is
really egregious conduct,

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:29.320
the prosecutors are probably
gonna bring out the big guns.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.080
- Time to bring out the big guns.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.590
- And one of the most egregious examples

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:35.030
of intentionally exposing
people to COVID-19

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:37.480
happened when Margaret
Cirko went to a supermarket

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:39.870
and started coughing and
spitting on the food.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.680
Cirko claimed to have the coronavirus,

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:45.650
and coughed or spit on
about $35,000 worth of food,

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:47.650
which had to be thrown out.

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:50.500
Authorities don't yet know
if Cirko really had COVID-19,

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.350
but her actions caused
serious losses to the store,

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:55.570
in addition to potentially
exposing employees

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:57.000
and shoppers to the virus.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.590
She was arrested and charged
with two felony counts

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:02.360
of terroristic threats,
one felony count of threats

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:05.090
to use a biological agent,
and one felony count

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:06.350
of criminal mischief.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.950
It's worth noting that it
probably doesn't matter

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:09.840
if she actually has the virus or not.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.840
For example, if you fire
an unloaded gun at someone,

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:15.080
but you think that gun is loaded,

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:18.280
that still generally
qualifies as attempted murder.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.680
Now, Cirko being cited
for threatening to spread

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.570
a biological agent brings us to whether

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:26.400
federal anti-terrorism laws
could apply to COVID-19.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:29.300
And on March 24th, Deputy
Attorney General Jeffrey Rosen

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:32.290
sent U.S. attorneys and federal
law enforcement agencies

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:34.960
a memo recommending that
people who purposefully expose

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:38.060
or infect others with
COVID-19 should be prosecuted

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:40.310
under federal terrorism statutes.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:42.460
Now, there are several federal statutes

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:43.780
that the DOJ is considering.

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:47.430
The first is 18 U.S.C. 2332 which makes it

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:49.910
a federal offense to
threaten or attempt to use

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:52.180
a weapon of mass
destruction against persons

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:54.710
within the United States, and
a weapon of mass destruction

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:57.500
is any weapon involving
a biological agent,

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:00.740
toxin, or a vector, and
biological agents are defined

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.210
to include viruses
capable of causing death,

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:06.400
disease, or other biological
malfunction in a human.

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.550
Now, a defense attorney
would probably argue that

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:11.040
the statute was intended to apply

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.390
to artificially created vectors,

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:16.000
and not the naturally occurring

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.410
cold viruses or coronaviruses.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.010
But the statute is written
broadly enough to apply,

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:23.410
and despite rumor-mongering
to the contrary,

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:25.730
there is no evidence that
COVID-19 was engineered

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:27.750
by China as a biological weapon,

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:31.010
but the statute probably still
brings it under its aegis.

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:34.370
Now, Rosen did not mention 18 U.S.C. 1365,

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:37.240
which penalizes tampering
with consumer products,

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.730
even though it arguably
applies to people like Cirko

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:42.190
who go around tampering
with consumer products.

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:45.430
However, this law was used
to arrest the mastermind

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:48.200
of the biggest bioterrorism
attack in U.S. history,

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.260
and could be useful in stopping people

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:52.050
from spreading COVID-19.

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:55.550
Now, this example is so crazy
it probably bears mentioning.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:59.090
In the early 1980s, Bhagwan
Rajneesh, also known as Osho,

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:02.010
amassed a number of devoted
religious followers in India,

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.760
moved to the United States,
took over an Oregon town,

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:06.740
fought with a co-founder of Nike,

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:08.810
acquired the largest
collection of Rolls-Royces

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.220
in the world, violated immigration laws,

